  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0321, and it contains five tables. The first table, General_User_Information, stores information about users, including their account, age, email, gender, name, password, phone number, and user ID. The second table, Member_Information, stores information about members, including their member ID, member level, status, validity end date, and validity start date. The third table, Team_Information, stores information about teams, including their team ID, team name, total team members, and team leader ID. The fourth table, Football_Player_Information, stores information about football players, including their affiliated team ID, football player ID, and primary key (football player ID and affiliated team ID). The fifth table, Match_Information, stores information about matches, including the away team ID, home team ID, match ID, match location, match result, match time, and primary key (match ID). The primary keys in each table are indicated by the PRIMARY KEY keyword. The foreign keys in each table are indicated by the FOREIGN KEY keyword, and they reference the primary keys in other tables. The update and delete rules for each foreign key are either CASCADE or RESTRICT.",
  "gold_question": "With the popularity of football worldwide, an increasing number of football enthusiasts and related organizations (such as football clubs and event organizers) are seeking dedicated social platforms to communicate, interact, participate in activities, track matches, and join memberships. A dedicated football social platform or membership management system can provide users with a centralized and comprehensive way to manage their social activities, match records, player/team profiles, and event interactions.\n\nSuch systems are not only suitable for the majority of football fans but can also serve football clubs, sponsors, and event organizers, assisting them in interacting with members, conducting marketing activities, managing event information, and providing personalized services. The main features include:\n\nUser registration and personal information management: including user basic information, social information (such as friends relationships), personal interests, etc.\nMembership management: allowing fans or users to become members and enjoy specific services, discounts, and activities.\nTeam management: users can create teams, join teams, and manage team information, etc.\nMatch management: including match schedules, match timelines, match results, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0321.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0321\nCREATE TABLE `general_user_information` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member_information` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `validity_start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `validity_end_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team_information` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `total_team_members` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team_leader_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `team_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_leader_id`) REFERENCES `general_user_information` (`user_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `football_player_information` (\n  `football_player_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `affiliated_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`football_player_id`, `affiliated_team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `player_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`affiliated_team_id`) REFERENCES `team_information` (`team_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `match_information` (\n  `match_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `home_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `away_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `match_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `match_result` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `match_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`match_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `match_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`home_team_id`) REFERENCES `team_information` (`team_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `match_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`away_team_id`) REFERENCES `team_information` (`team_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
